ipal parts"}, {"id": "e62af5a7-ccbf-4137-a83d-6982c0e5f95a", "type": "concept", "title": "Active recall, reading exposure, and review cycles"}], "description": "Students build high-frequency recognition with long-term retention."}, {"id": "90506e9b-3b96-4c87-bb65-f8468972e4c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Word formation", "children": [{"id": "ed2be40d-401d-4277-a7d3-028b4e95cf70", "type": "concept", "title": "Hebrew roots, stems, nouns, adjectives, and derived forms"}, {"id": "01e55a0a-0ee0-440b-ac0e-2baf1d07be51", "type": "concept", "title": "Greek compounds, prefixes, suffixes, and verbal stems"}, {"id": "fb63c219-4f31-4741-89c5-e90030eaae15", "type": "concept", "title": "Loanwords, names, and transliterated terms"}], "description": "The point is to see how words are built and related."}, {"id": "15ecde85-d9d8-43b0-81b3-580050a5cf67", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Semantic range", "children": [{"id": "55b3ff50-6e3f-4764-a3db-0050af2cf093", "type": "concept", "title": "Lexical domain, usage, collocation, metaphor, and genre"}, {"id": "49408f82-9e06-4834-afe0-46134e591efa", "type": "concept", "title": "Polysemy, idiom, and context-sensitive meaning"}, {"id": "a565abcd-6706-4dd5-8ef0-e7be2173b20f", "type": "concept", "title": "Word-study fallacies and safeguards"}], "description": "Students move beyond one-word glosses."}]}, {"id": "e58130f7-9d6d-44bd-bdca-180a481c2456", "type": "topic", "title": "Hebrew Nominal System: Nouns, Adjectives, Pronouns, Construct Chains, and Prepositions", "description": "This module studies how Biblical Hebrew builds phrases and relationships through gender, number, state, agreement, pronominal suffixes, and particles.", "children": [{"id": "0d0cbbaa-c7b5-48d3-a851-cb9ed83b890f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nouns and adjectives", "children": [{"id": "5fb8fc73-61c2-493c-8409-5de388137ae8", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender, number, definiteness, state, and agreement"}, {"id": "04f832d9-bbf8-43a6-99db-69fae19c773a", "type": "concept", "title": "Adjective position and attributive/predicative function"}, {"id": "54555a46-82e8-48f3-9f5f-2d962c5a3df1", "type": "concept", "title": "Irregular nouns and common patterns"}], "description": "Students learn how Hebrew marks relationships in phrases."}, {"id": "93b81160-5220-416c-ad12-65567967fe87", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Construct chains", "children": [{"id": "411ffbbf-150a-4870-9472-997a007a52d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Construct and absolute states"}, {"id": "ff5a8407-e61c-467a-b722-98989af27015", "type": "concept", "title": "Possession, relationship, titles, and abstract constructions"}, {"id": "72ec2245-a6ee-48a6-b80b-fa7797b74786", "type": "concept", "title": "Translation choices for multi-word chains"}], "description": "The gist is to interpret one of Hebrew's most important phrase structures."}, {"id": "b7582c57-7d06-4643-8d2c-38d72ffe971a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pronouns and prepositions", "children": [{"id": "adec1deb-5350-4d13-a1a4-3672b6b2e25b", "type": "concept", "title": "Independent pronouns, pronominal suffixes, demonstratives, relatives, and interrogatives"}, {"id": "848a53c9-799d-442e-ac14-2415bc98f537", "type": "concept", "title": "Prefixed and independent prepositions"}, {"id": "cd45ff42-207c-492b-8888-fee33db824f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Particles, negation, and common idioms"}], "description": "Students identify compact forms that carry major interpretive weight."}]}, {"id": "4ef93e49-1bd1-42a1-b607-d62f3d7e578c", "type": "topic", "title": "Hebrew Verbal System: Binyanim, Perfect, Imperfect, Participles, Infinitives, and Weak Verbs", "description": "Students learn the central engine of Biblical Hebrew narrative, poetry, command, aspect, and clause flow.", "children": [{"id": "2cc7c29a-83ab-4dad-8968-eabc403856fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strong verb system", "children": [{"id": "12c792bd-2d31-4abb-8362-afafb3e68921", "type": "concept", "title": "Qal, Niphal, Piel, Pual, Hiphil, Hophal, and Hithpael"},