507a7-6858-495f-89db-287ce58d7aa0", "type": "topic", "title": "Translation Method: Literal, Literary, Functional, Theological, and Annotated Translation", "description": "Students learn translation as disciplined interpretation, balancing accuracy, readability, genre, audience, and transparent annotation.", "children": [{"id": "df0a8815-a71f-4f2c-be6d-e397cdd89727", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Translation philosophies", "children": [{"id": "cea2f592-5556-453b-9ed8-6c12074d0689", "type": "concept", "title": "Formal equivalence, functional equivalence, literary translation, and paraphrase"}, {"id": "5564fa5e-a407-4300-a2a9-031f599ec724", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience, genre, register, and readability"}, {"id": "ee1439b4-b895-4f13-bbdb-aab125cc0d1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Translation committees and theological stakes"}], "description": "Students learn why translations differ."}, {"id": "fde73c6c-a90d-407d-b646-f2e779b4af2b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Decision-making process", "children": [{"id": "9e034df7-98ce-4ace-a352-0bf86626ebcb", "type": "concept", "title": "Parsing, syntax, lexical range, context, genre, and intertextuality"}, {"id": "f6bc870c-5dff-4383-a61a-3be9211faf14", "type": "concept", "title": "Ambiguity, idiom, metaphor, and culturally embedded terms"}, {"id": "0fe4030b-b8d7-464e-bad2-0d682f0a08ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Footnotes, brackets, and explanatory comments"}], "description": "The point is to make translation choices visible and defensible."}, {"id": "a70b7ce6-2aeb-4df9-92bf-45eda6b9621a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparing translations", "children": [{"id": "caecc4e2-c5bc-4715-bbba-a54832a28dcb", "type": "concept", "title": "Major English translations and their philosophies"}, {"id": "729446ad-9842-400e-840f-99d9db87e0b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Hebrew Bible, Septuagint, and New Testament comparison"}, {"id": "2f7def58-fcce-42b1-838e-d1759bb7a02a", "type": "concept", "title": "Detecting interpretive decisions in wording"}], "description": "Students use published translations as evidence, not shortcuts."}]}, {"id": "96d6c488-2b2a-4653-a2b7-c37b30c5f450", "type": "topic", "title": "Lexicons, Grammars, Concordances, Corpora, and Digital Language Tools", "description": "This topic trains students to use reference tools critically rather than mechanically, including lexicons, grammars, parsers, concordances, corpora, and databases.", "children": [{"id": "37e96990-65a7-4b93-ae4b-81460ca5c847", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lexicon use", "children": [{"id": "1ce3ba2b-f13d-492d-96fe-c4c583603f2b", "type": "concept", "title": "HALOT, BDB, BDAG, LSJ, glosses, entries, citations, and semantic domains"}, {"id": "1d5b41da-53c6-4830-be71-0ef7bc7f935e", "type": "concept", "title": "Root fallacies, etymological fallacies, and selective evidence"}, {"id": "dcd4f542-d3cb-49b3-80c2-e7cbda9bc4a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Choosing a meaning from usage and context"}], "description": "Students learn to use dictionaries responsibly."}, {"id": "5cbd2890-0808-4788-af6b-28f569008a96", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grammar and concordance workflow", "children": [{"id": "3c930fb1-3d52-4638-a038-06045b10a2bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Reference grammars, syntax guides, concordances, cross-references, and indices"}, {"id": "0c4a3457-a389-45b3-8978-c3326184ffc5", "type": "concept", "title": "When to consult a grammar versus a lexicon"}, {"id": "7bdd93c7-d3c8-42e9-9edc-478ec8b13dfa", "type": "concept", "title": "Documenting evidence in notes"}], "description": "The gist is to build a reliable reference process."}, {"id": "a9381923-f176-4335-90ef-32a41885600a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital tools", "children": [{"id": "15be41d3-46e5-4d27-9a4f-8d42c5324c14", "type": "concept", "title": "Sefaria, STEP Bible, Blue Letter Bible, Bible software, corpora, and morphology databases"}, {"id": "e79e87c8-70d4-47de-8a55-a0d862f31b76", "type": "concept", "title": "Parsers, tagged texts, searches, and exportable notes"}, {"id": "b6d39506-8cfb-4896-bebf-7e46238641c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Verification, bias, licensing, and citation"}], "description": "Students learn to benefit from software while retaining language judgment."}]}, {"id": "cae8ff16-083d-4ae0-8411-ccf1b528fc37", "type": "topic", "title": "Textual Criticism, Manuscripts, Variants, Apparatus, Masoretic Text, Septuagint, and New Testament Witnesses", "description": "Students learn how textual witnesses and apparatus entries affect translation and interpretation without reducing scripture to uncertainty.", "children": [{"id": "2d6f10ae-63d5-429b-945a-f81c2f9eeb14", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Manuscript traditions", "children": [{"id": "3007689a-c8d6-450b-9601-f3a891c7bbdd", "type": "concept", "title": "Masoretic Text, Dead Sea Scrolls, Samaritan Pentateuch, Septuagint, Vulgate, Peshitta, and Targums"}, {"id": "f02c1198-8c53-47e6-8581-ed40db4adf21", "type": "concept", "title": "Papyri, uncials, minuscules, lectionaries, and patristic citations"}, {"id": "f5cd71b8-cc9a-4c26-9d9f-abb608100260", "type": "concept", "title": "Transmission, scribes, and communities"}], "description": "Students learn where printed texts come from."}, {"id": "e5a9e95c-9567-4fdc-9402-f370812430f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Apparatus skills", "children": [{"id": "08a6ece0-5e9c-417e-8a68-cb4e91286325", "type": "concept", "title": "Sigla, witnesses, variants, conjectures, omissions, additions, and orthographic differences"}, {"id": "bd81db3a-277c-41cd-ace8-1953983cdcd0", "type": "concept", "title": "BHS/BHQ apparatus and Nestle-Aland apparatus"}, {"id": "63de6d07-3374-43de-b6ea-960de717dda6", "type": "concept", "title": "External and internal evidence"}], "description": "The point is to read critical notes without panic."}, {"id": "92566488-4a0b-4580-9309-4b8a48edd5bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interpretive impact", "children": [{"id": "198d1e2b-9942-4471-83b6-7ed2efe76598", "type": "concept", "title": "Meani